  reads telemetry, never writes; server path fails open.\n- **Retirement policy** (reversible, retired_at-only, never DELETE; --dry-run + --audit-out; owns the\n  library filesystem): (a) N=2 stale over â‰¥2 DISTINCT probe-days â†’ retire; (b) never-surfaced AND\n  interest_score < AURORA_RETIRE_MIN_INTEREST (0.3) AND older than AURORA_RETIRE_AGE_DAYS (60) â†’ retire.\n  Wired into `run-morning-briefing.cmd` (not a new task â€” task reg needs elevation).\n- **EXECUTE â†’ gate (1026) â†’ 2 reviewers (A GO; B GO+1 MAJOR) â†’ fix iter 1 â†’ re-gate (1029) â†’ re-review GO.**\n- **MAJOR fixed (the key catch):** the stale rule originally used the top-2 link_health rows by\n  timestamp with no inter-probe-day gate, so the W3 activation's same-day probes would have retired\n  **7 live artifacts tonight** â€” contradicting the spec's \"armed, not demonstrated (~2 weeks of probe\n  history)\". Fixed: require 2 DISTINCT stale probe-days. **Independently verified on the LIVE KB\n  (read-only): stale_candidates 7â†’0, cold_candidates 0, local skills 822-824 protected â€” nothing\n  retires tonight.** New tests lock the masked same-day case.\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` â†’ 1029 passed (was 1009; +20). No live retirement run. KB backups retained.\n\n### Wave 4 â€” The taste score â€” âœ… GREEN (2026-06-10)\n\n- **Status:** converged with 0 fix-iterations (both reviewers GO; only non-blocking MINORs); committed.\n  Live activation done (migration applied + supervised LLM run).\n- **Files:** `roles/taste.py` (new â€” `resolve_taste_model`, `score_one`, `heuristic_score`, `run` nightly\n  leg + cap + degrade-to-heuristic, `ensure_scored`/`score_pending` on-demand), `kb/migrations/0025_interest_score.sql`\n  (+ `kb/schema.sql` mirror: `interest_score REAL`, `interest_why TEXT`, `interest_scored_at TEXT`),\n  `kb/pricing.yaml` (`default_models.taste` â†’ `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001`, already priced $1/$5 verified),\n  `docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md` (new â€” John-editable taste profile)