tifacts (fixture-tested); papers matchable-and-labeled in HH pull (fixture-tested), models scoped\nper D1; all backfills ran with audits saved; plugin rebuilt + handed to John for reinstall + smoked\nafter reinstall; clean committed tree; `python -m pytest` green.\n\n- **Given** an arxiv URL in any sweep, **when** screened, **then** kind='paper' â€” no path mints an arxiv tool/agent (fixture-tested per sweep).\n- **Given** a crates.io/pypi/npm tool URL, **when** screened, **then** it is NOT rejected by the source gate (allowlist regression test). [SUBTLE â€” the false-positive trap]\n- **Given** a drained discovery_queue item with â‰¥10 markdown links and no installable-content markers, **then** its links are re-enqueued (INSERT OR IGNORE) and no artifact row is created.\n- **Given** `AURORA_SECURITY_MODE` unset (production), **when** the snapshot builds, **then** a retired artifact's page is absent. [SUBTLE â€” the dead-code-placement trap, E20]\n- **Given** a pull query matching a paper, **then** it is returned with kind='paper' visibly labeled and is never auto-loaded; **given** a single-mode query, **then** no model row is routed or recorded as surfaced. [D1/D2]\n- **Given** the backfill runs twice, **then** the second run is a no-op (idempotent dir-moves and re-kinds; audit shows zero changes).\n\n## Wave 3 â€” Weekly digest v1 + notability signal\n\n**Intent:** Ship the human-facing digest (papers' only push surface â€” criterion 6) and light up the\nalready-built-but-never-scheduled link-health probe so stars/staleness exist as signals.\n\n**PRECONDITION (MANUAL/environmental):** authenticated gh CLI â€” verify `& 'C:\\Program Files\\GitHub\nCLI\\gh.exe' auth status` before the backfill; HALT-AND-ASK John if unauthenticated (unauthenticated\nis 60 req/hr â€” a multi-hour stall; the authenticated path is minutes).\n\n**Deliverables:** `bin/setup-tasks.ps1` registers `bin/check_link_health.py` as a weekly scheduled\ntask (idempotent registration, mirroring the 