ds + any unscored artifact reaching a serving surface â€” never the full back catalog.\n\n**Deliverables:** `kb/pricing.yaml`: priced key for the chosen taste model (+ `verification:` block,\n`verified:false` permitted) and a `default_models.taste` entry; `roles/taste.py` resolves its model\nfrom `default_models.taste` with `AURORA_TASTE_MODEL` env override â€” a unit test asserts the\nresolved tag has a non-zero priced rate (extends `tests/test_pricing_keys.py`). Migration\n`kb/migrations/0025_interest_score.sql` (additive; next free number, verified; mirror in\n`kb/schema.sql`): `artifacts.interest_score REAL`, `interest_why TEXT`, `interest_scored_at TEXT`.\n`docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md`: versioned, John-editable profile (Claude/agent ecosystem; usable >\nacademic; novelty over volume) â€” seeded in this wave, edited only by John thereafter.\n`roles/taste.py`: scorer for (a) new non-paper, non-retired finds nightly and (b) any unscored\nartifact that becomes a top_finds/digest candidate (so serving surfaces never rank NULL-scored\nrows); inputs short_description + incorporation_note + `gh_stargazers` + kind; every call metered\nthrough CostRecorder; nightly call cap (env `AURORA_TASTE_NIGHTLY_CAP`, default 40) with heuristic\nfallback (stars+badge+kind-priority, persisted as the score with NULL `interest_why`) when capped or\non LLM failure; wired into the orchestrator post-librarian step. Precedence: `interest_why` drives\nranking surfaces; `incorporation_note` stays the library \"how to incorporate\" voice. Ranking switch:\ntop_finds (morning_briefing) + weekly digest order by `interest_score` (any residual NULL sorts\nbelow scored, then the Wave-1 heuristic as tiebreak); why-lines upgrade to `interest_why` when present.\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 3\n\n**done-when:** Checkable ON DEMAND inside the build: a supervised capped run of `roles/taste.py`\nover K existing unscored serving-surface candidates produces `interest_score` + `interest_why` with\nnon-zero metered cost rows (â‰¤ the cap); fixture tests prove cap/fallback/ranking behavior; top finds\n+ digest order by the score; the profile doc exists and is referenced; clean committed tree;\n`python -m pytest` green. **SEPARATELY-VERIFIED (armed, not demonstrated in-build):** the nightly\nleg â€” every new find from subsequent nightly runs arrives scored; verified by John from the next\nmorning's data, mirroring the Wave-5 fixture-based pattern.\n\n- **Given** a taste call, **then** its `costs` row prices against the same tag taste.py resolved (no $0 fiction). [SUBTLE â€” the unpriced-tag trap, E17]\n- **Given** the nightly cap is hit or the LLM fails, **then** remaining finds get the heuristic score persisted + NULL `interest_why` (no crash, no unscored-and-unranked rows).\n- **Given** a scored and an unscored artifact, **then** ranking places scored-by-interest first, falling back to the Wave-1 heuristic â€” never raw recency alone; **given** a top_finds/digest candidate with NULL score, **then** it is scored (LLM or heuristic) before surfacing.\n\n## Wave 5 â€” Close the loop\n\n**Intent:** Usage shifts what surfaces (criterion 4), the catalog self-maintains (criterion 5), and\nthe digest shows John whether Aurora is actually helping.\n\n**Deliverables:** Bounded usage modifier in the HH server `_compute_matches` (server.py:629-683,\npost-cosine â€” the repetition gate at lines 779-824 is the read-telemetry-at-match-time precedent):\nper-artifact boost from `loaded` history, decay from `dismissed`; **bound = Â±0.10 on the cosine\nscore (decided), exponential time decay with a 30-day half-life (decided)**; same modifier applied\nin top_finds + digest ranking on top of interest_score; fixture-tested both sides; plugin rebuild +\nreinstall (MANUAL â€” John) + smoke. Retirement policy (`bin/retirement_policy.py`, nightly, audited,\nreversible): N=2 consecutive stale probes (link_health is append-per-probe â€” E8) â†’ retire;\nnever-surfaced AND `interest_score < AURORA_RETIRE_MIN_INTEREST` (default 0.3) AND older than\n`AURORA_RETIRE_AGE_DAYS` (default 60) â†’ retire (env-overridable defaults; the defaults are the\ndecision); **acceptance is fixture-based** (live stale-retirements need ~2 weeks of probe history\nby design; the live leg is armed, not demonstrated). Digest value section: suggestion-adoption\ntrend, loads/dismissals this week, profile-drift hints (most-dismissed kinds/domains vs profile\nemphases â†’ prompts a manual `INTEREST_PROFILE.md` edit; NO auto-mutation).\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 4\n\n**done-when:** Fixture hh_events demonstrably shift both HH match ranking and top-finds order (tests\nprove boost + decay + the Â±0.10 bound); the retirement policy runs nightly unattended with\nfixture-proven rules and the live leg armed (N=2, threshold/age defaults set); the digest shows the\nvalue section; plugin rebuilt + handed to John for reinstall + smoked after reinstall; clean\ncommitted tree; `python -m pytest` green.\n\n- **Given** an artifact with loaded history, **then** its match score rises by at most 0.10; **given** dismissed history, it falls by at most 0.10; **given** 30-day-old events, the effect is halved. [SUBTLE â€” unbounded feedback trap]\n- **Given** a fixture artifact with 2 consecutive stale probes, **then** the policy retires it (audited); **given** only 1, it does not.\n- **Given** a week of usage, **then** the digest's value section reports adoption trend + loads/dismissals and surfaces drift hints without modifying the profile.\n","numLines":223,"startLine":1,"totalLines":223}}}
